      "body": "## Motivation\n\nMooncake PD disaggregation raises `ValueError: DSA tail slot index missing: src=[], dst=[...]` when Prefill and Decode disagree on whether a DSA tail slot exists.\n\nPrefill's last chunk indexed `DSA_TAIL` with `min(extend_end, len(origin_input_ids))`. Decode registers `len(origin_input_ids)` (`_rebootstrap_prefill_len`). Empty vs non-empty is only `seq_len % pool_size` (usually 4). When `extend_end` sits on a pool boundary and the prompt length is one past it, Prefill emits `[]` and Decode emits a live 6-tuple such as `[req_pool_idx, 0, 1, 0, 0, 12]` (`tail_extra_slots=8`). C128 already uses `transfer_input_len` for this request-scoped contract. KV page indices are unchanged.\n\nFixes #46763\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Last-chunk `DSA_TAIL` now uses `transfer_input_len` (`len(origin_input_ids)`), matching Decode and C128.\n- Token-pool payloads still use the materialized range `min(extend_end, transfer_input_len)`.\n- CPU unit test covers the pool-boundary mismatch (old index empty + transfer raises; new index transfers), a sampled token past origin, and a pool-aligned prompt that stays empty on both sides.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNo model-forward change. `test/registered/unit/disaggregation/test_dsa_tail_transfer.py` fails on the previous index and passes after this change.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format touched files with ruff\n- [x] Add a unit test for the last-chunk length mismatch\n- [ ] Documentation update not required\n- [ ] Accuracy and speed benchmarks not applicable\n- [x] Follow existing disaggregation state-transfer style\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40469818288](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40469818288)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40469818284](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40469818284)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40469818181](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40469818181)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
